A||||14||Cooter||Alright Lawyers- time to help the kids! (long)||||1||
Z||000000||Cooter||10-26-2001||10:20 PM||||At my school, the lunch program has really gone to $hit lately. According to what we are told- federal law dictates that the lunchroom is a completly seperate entity (sp?) from the school. The school administration has no control over what happens in the lunchroom...BUT:<BR>We are told now that a child with no lunch money CAN NOT charge a lunch to their account. They must put the lunch away and call home for lunch money. If no one can bring money RIGHT THEN, the school (which is supposed to be completly seperate from the lunch room) is responsible for picking up the cost of the lunch. Our PTO is now completly broke because of the lunch room not keeping up with sending the parents a notice about kids owing money.<BR>Today, a kid got too many french fries so he had to remove a portion of them- to the trash can! They took food off his plate and threw it away! "It is a federal law about portion size."<BR>One of my students was told she could not eat until someone brought her lunch money. I got pissed- don't tell a child that they can't have lunch! We keep hearing this is federal law, but I can't imagine a law somewhere that keeps hungry kids from having lunch. We serve a lower socio-economic community and get a lot of federal assistance (Title programs, breakfast, Early Bird etc...) so I don't understand why they are suddenly being so mean to the kids about this. <BR>Someone with Federal Law experience, PLEASE try to find out what is going on- I would hate to go to jail for smacking the lunch room manager when she takes the plate away from my children.||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroMontreal||10-26-2001||10:49 PM||||That Sucks!||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroMontreal||10-26-2001||10:49 PM||||Thats Disgusting actually!||||reg||1
Z||000003||84fierotrevor||10-26-2001||10:56 PM||||oh god let them throw my lunch room food away that stuff is so sick !<BR>the one day i thought we had some food that wanst old yucky moldy or hiary was the day we got these little frozen taco bell burittos every one was all happy<BR>untell i read the lable that said throw away after januray 1996 and this was in 1999<BR>god ! i hate school lunch food i wish parents would just take the time to pack there children a lunch it only takes a few minutes.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cooter||10-26-2001||11:23 PM||||As if the above was not bad enough-<BR>The kids have to serve themselves. THis would not be bad for big kids- but when kindergarten kids go through the line, they are shorter than the sneeze shields so what ever they cough out goes in the food. I've seen the little ones wipe their nose on the hand and then grab the spoon for some smashed potatoes. Then some other kid knocks the spoon in the vat 'o' taters and all that happens is the spoon gets wiped off and put back in service.<BR>New this year is the system of making the kids wipe down their tables after eating. This is just wrong! A five year old should not have to wash tables- if they make a mess then clean up after themselves but not clean up after a whole class.<BR>I have not eaten in the "crapeteria" in 2 weeks and today I get a bill for lunch money that I owe. Then we get an email from the lunch room manager saying that under federal law, soda cans are not permitted in the cafeteria. Two weeks ago, the price for an employee lunch goes up to 50 cents higher than a child's meal but lunchroom workers eat for free!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||10-26-2001||11:46 PM||||Here's my wife's input (H.S. phys/chem teacher in GA.)<P>She said she has also heard that lunches couldn't be charged, any more. But she's never heard of denying a kid lunch.<BR>As for taking food off a child's plate?<BR>That's just being an a$$hole. Federal law or not.<BR>And since when did kids get to serve themselves? Kids are gonna grab as much or more than they can eat. Adults ought to be serving the kids.<BR>As for the lunchroom workers eating free?<BR>She said that she doesn't know about AL, but in GA, lunchroom workers get paid squat. If they get free food, big deal. Not like it's gourmet food anyway. <BR>I don't understand why YOU got billed, though, even if you haven't eaten there.<P>A 5-year old cleaning up after a whole class?<BR>Why? Was this a punishment? I don't think that it would be bad to make the kids clean up after themselves, but not the whole class.<P><BR>My wife loves to teach. Loves her kids, but she despises all the beauracracy and administrative B.S. If she ever quits, that'll be why.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 10-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||ray b||10-27-2001||12:02 AM||||ask the laws # section subsection ect<BR>some people make up federal rules on the fly to cover their rear. if they have a real law # look it up and read it on the net<BR>check with pta or teachers unions national web sites for new laws about schools and lunch<BR>AND NO RON ketchup is not a vegie some laws are needed most are not!!!!!<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000007||maryjane||10-27-2001||12:23 AM||||I agree with RayB. Schoolboards are notorious for using any vague law to their advantage, even ones that don't apply in their districts. In Texas, a schoolboard's decision is virtually untouchable, their word is law, short of a recall election. Closed to the public meetings are common. They can even choose to do away with our homestead exemption. Cafeteria supervisors are nearly as bad. Fried liver. ughh!||||reg||1
Z||000008||Cooter||10-27-2001||09:08 AM||||I think the biggest problem is the lunchroom manager and poor book keeping. Since I started teaching there, the working staff in the L/R has had at least 4 complete groups of people come and go- we are talking about a large number of people who just leave because of her. They get written up for stupid stuff- she had to attend anger management classes and stuff like that, but nobody can stand her.<BR>As far as the book keeping- the kids are supposed to get a notice saying they need lunch money before they run out. My kid that I payed the lunch money for did not get a notice. Even with a $0.00 account balance, they did not give her the "URGENT URGENT URGENT!!!! YOUR CHILD NEEDS LUNCH MONEY!!! NO LUNCHES CAN BE CHARGED" notice. So, what if she forgets to tell her mom that she needs lunch money? On Monday, I am probably going to confront the manager if she takes the plate away from the child. At the beginning of the school year, I made a promise to the parents to take care of their children the best that I could- that includes making sure they get fed. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Raydar||10-27-2001||10:34 AM||||Good luck. I feel for ya'. Wish I could help.<P>Raydar||||reg||9
Z||000010||Oreif||10-27-2001||11:03 AM||||OK being a parent this concerns me. So I did a little searching.<BR>Here is the National Lunch Program Website:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fns.usda.gov/cnd/Lunch/default.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fns.usda.gov/cnd/Lunch/default.htm</A> <P>I would contact them with what is going on a see if the "crapateria" is really following federal regulations.<P>Here are all the different nutrition programs that the government sponsors.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fns.usda.gov/cnd/Lunch/Governance/Policy/ImplementPubLaw105-336.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fns.usda.gov/cnd/Lunch/Governance/Policy/ImplementPubLaw105-336.htm</A> <P><BR>Here is your State contact that governs the school lunch programs.<BR>Alabama NSLP, CACFP, SFSP<BR>State Director<BR>Child Nutrition Programs<BR>Alabama Department of Education<BR>Gordon Persons Building<BR>50 North Ripley Street, Room 5301<BR>Montgomery, Alabama 36130-2101<BR>Phone: 334-242-1988<BR>Fax: 334-242-2475<P>Here is the USDA's Hotline info:<BR>"We will not hesitate to remove violators, and to prosecute the individuals who intentionally violate program rules.  If you are concerned that program funds are misused, contact USDA:"<P>USDA Hotline <BR>Office of Inspector General<BR>Post Office Box 23399<BR>Washington, D.C.  20026-3399<BR>Tel 202-690-1622 <BR>Toll Free 800-424-9121 <BR>TDD 202-690-1202 <P>This is their "Team Nutrition" Program's website: <A HREF="http://www.fns.usda.gov/tn/Default.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fns.usda.gov/tn/Default.htm</A> <P>I hope these help. From what you say is going on, I'd be angry too.<BR>Maybe it would be helpful to get other teachers and parents together to correct the problems. Hopefully the first link above can assist in correcting the problems.<P>------------------<BR>                <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">              <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 10-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||isthiswhereiputausername?||10-27-2001||01:45 PM||||it looks like some of your "crapeteria" workers enjoy their job too much.. working in a school, (even a cafeteria) one of the job requirments should be to like kids.. <P>It dont sound like they like kids too much..<BR>I also agree with that 6 year olds are too young to server themselves.. <P>but to refuse lunches and to take food off a plate and toss it out, is crazy! <P>Keep us informed how it works out for you there Cooter!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Cooter||10-27-2001||07:58 PM||||Thanks Oreif! I am printing the documents from the first website now and will highlight anything that looks like what we are violating. If nothing else, a call to the state department should get someone to come check on the situation.||||reg||1
Z||000013||maryjane||10-28-2001||03:01 AM||||Sounds like you might need to get ALL the parents a little more involved. If a good majority of the students are underpriviledged or economically strained, perhaps they can get their representatives involved. I know it sounds dumb to say write your congressman/woman, but I have had good luck in the past. The parents are voters after all, and no politician wants to be branded that they let students in their district go without lunch. We forgive foreign debts by the billions and it really irks me to hear about things like you describe, here at home. But you have to get THEM to do it along with you, it carries more weight if the numbers of people writing are high.Check with schools outside your district and see if they have a similar problem. Maybe there is mishandling of funds or even stealing of food products involved. I've seen cases here where the schools in upper-class neighborhoods actually got more federal/state funding than the poorer (the ones that really need it) area schools, simply because the better schools had the where-with-all to find every available federal grant and entitlement.||||reg||1
Z||000014||fierohoho||10-29-2001||06:33 AM||||Don't forget the American Civil Liberties Union (A.C.L.U)<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lightbar.gif"> ||||reg||1
